# BearerMail: headers taken off mail OUR users send (submission port only —
# the `subcleanup` service in master.cf; mail arriving from outside keeps its
# headers untouched).
#
# The Received: line Postfix writes on submission names the container the web
# and phone apps send from and its internal address. Nobody receiving the mail
# needs that, and spam filters do not use it: they judge the server that hands
# the message over (Mailjet's, or this one's public address when sending
# direct), checked against SPF, DKIM and DMARC. Gmail and Proton drop the same
# hop. X-Originating-IP and the mail-program headers go for the same reason.
/^Received:/            IGNORE
/^X-Originating-IP:/    IGNORE
/^X-Mailer:/            IGNORE
/^User-Agent:/          IGNORE
